  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION AND CONSERVATION OF SUMATRAN TIGER IN KERINCI SEBLAT NATIONAL PARK, SUMATRA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) FURTHER REDUCE THREATS TO TIGER, TIGER PREY SPECIES AND HABITAT THROUGH SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL (SMART) FOREST PATROLS, INVESTIGATIONS, HUMAN-TIGER CONFLICT MITIGATION AND WILDLIFE AND FOREST LAW ENFORCEMENT (2) MITIGATE HUMAN-TIGER CONFLICTS TO PROTECT BOTH TIGER AND FOREST-EDGE COMMUNITIES AND (3) INCREASE KNOWLEDGE AND INSTITUTIONAL CAPACITY TO CONSERVE TIGER AND OTHER ENDANGERED SPECIES AMONG LOCAL AND NATIONAL GOVERNMENT AGENCIES, CIVIL SOCIETY, LOCAL DECISION MAKERS, RELIGIOUS LEADERS, AND TRADITIONAL COMMUNITIES.</narrative>
  </description>
